  "Derived by measurement: a row is mined only when the translator reported the quotation verbatim AND the block contains a 30-character run of that verse (or a quoted span of 10+ characters that is a substring of it), compared with quotation marks and punctuation stripped. adapted/self rows and 17 unconfirmed verbatim claims (mostly one-word or short-phrase echoes) are self_rendered. 148 of 299 rows mined.",
  "Conventions: curly quotation marks mirror the English; reader/hearer address तुम (precedent all-of-grace.hi, the-way-to-god.hi); 'conversion' मन-फिराव (37 of 43 sites, the shipped hi corpus's majority term); author name बैक्सटर (library form); the book's refrain 'Turn ye, turn ye, why will ye die?' quotes IRV Ezekiel 33:11.",
